# task 07 string_append — expected output: 750000
# build: unicon -s 07_string_append.icn    run: 07_string_append.exe
# `text := text || "x"` is the spec's own form, but it is *not* the quadratic cell the task
# is designed to measure here: measured 90-136 ms for the 750000 appends, and linear in the
# append count — 47 / 94 / 172 ms at 250000 / 500000 / 1000000, and still linear with the
# accumulator declared `global` or the append moved into a procedure. Unicon's concatenation
# therefore extends the accumulator in place rather than copying it, so the cell measures an
# amortised extend. The deviation is recorded in RUN.md, the same one the AutoHotkey, Dyalog,
# Lobster, Erlang and Elixir rows carry.
# timing: &time is Unicon's wall clock in milliseconds since midnight, and &errout is
#         the standard error stream, so TIME_MS goes to stderr and stdout is unchanged.

procedure main()
    ssT0 := &time
    text := ""
    every i := 1 to 750000 do
        text := text || "x"
    write(&errout, "TIME_MS=", &time - ssT0)
    write(*text)
end
